{"id":"mahabharata-1-198","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":198,"title":"अष्टनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 198 · Vidura is sent to bring the Pandavas","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra accepts the advice and sends Vidura to Drupada's city with gifts to bring back the Pandavas, Kunti and Draupadi. Vidura is welcomed by Drupada, Krishna and the Pandavas and delivers the invitation.","kn":"ಸಲಹೆಯನ್ನು ಒಪ್ಪಿದ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಪಾಂಡವರು, ಕುಂತಿ, ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯನ್ನು ಕರೆತರಲು ಉಡುಗೊರೆಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ವಿದುರನನ್ನು ದ್ರುಪದನ ನಗರಕ್ಕೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದ್ರುಪದ, ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣ, ಪಾಂಡವರು ವಿದುರನನ್ನು ಸ್ವಾಗತಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅವನು ಆಹ್ವಾನ ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र सलाह मानकर विदुर को उपहारों के साथ द्रुपद की नगरी भेजते हैं ताकि पाण्डवों, कुन्ती और द्रौपदी को ले आएँ। द्रुपद, श्रीकृष्ण और पाण्डव विदुर का स्वागत करते हैं और वे निमन्त्रण देते हैं।","te":"సలహాను అంగీకరించిన ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు పాండవులను, కుంతిని, ద్రౌపదిని తీసుకురావడానికి కానుకలతో విదురుని ద్రుపదుని నగరానికి పంపుతాడు. ద్రుపదుడు, శ్రీకృష్ణుడు, పాండవులు విదురునికి స్వాగతం పలుకుతారు, అతడు ఆహ్వానం అందిస్తాడు.","ta":"அறிவுரையை ஏற்ற திருதராஷ்டிரன் பாண்டவர்களையும் குந்தியையும் திரௌபதியையும் அழைத்து வரப் பரிசுகளுடன் விதுரரைத் த்ருபதனின் நகருக்கு அனுப்புகிறான். த்ருபதனும் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரும் பாண்டவர்களும் விதுரரை வரவேற்க, அவர் அழைப்பைத் தெரிவிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ഉപദേശം സ്വീകരിച്ച്, പാണ്ഡവരെയും കുന്തിയെയും ദ്രൗപദിയെയും തിരികെ കൊണ്ടുവരാൻ വിദുരരെ സമ്മാനങ്ങളുമായി ദ്രുപദന്റെ നഗരത്തിലേക്ക് അയയ്ക്കുന്നു. ദ്രുപദനും കൃഷ്ണനും പാണ്ഡവരും വിദുരരെ സ്വീകരിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹം ക്ഷണം അറിയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.198; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"विदुरागमनपर्व","titleEn":"Viduragamana Parva (Vidura's coming)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भीष्मः शांतनवो विद्वान्द्रोणश्च भगवानृषिः ।\nहितं परमकं वाक्यं त्वं च सत्यं ब्रवीषि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma son of Shantanu, the learned one, and the holy sage Drona have given supreme and beneficial counsel, and you too speak the truth to me."}},{"n":2,"text":"यथैव पाण्डोस्ते वीराः कुन्तीपुत्रा महारथाः ।\nतथैव धर्मतः सर्वे मम पुत्रा न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the heroic sons of Kunti, great chariot-warriors, are Pandu's sons, so by dharma they are all my sons too; there is no doubt."}},{"n":3,"text":"यथैव मम पुत्राणामिदं राज्यं विधीयते ।\nतथैव पाण्डुपुत्राणामिदं राज्यं न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As this kingdom is meant for my sons, so it is meant for the sons of Pandu; there is no doubt."}},{"n":4,"text":"क्षत्तरानय गच्छैतान्सह मात्रा सुसत्कृतान् ।\nतया च देवरूपिण्या कृष्णया सह भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kshattri, go and bring them here with all honor, together with their mother and with Krishna, who is like a goddess in form, O Bharata."}},{"n":5,"text":"दिष्ट्या जीवन्ति ते पार्था दिष्ट्या जीवति सा पृथा ।\nदिष्ट्या द्रुपदकन्यां च लब्धवन्तो महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune the Parthas live, by good fortune Pritha lives, and by good fortune the great warriors have won the daughter of Drupada."}},{"n":6,"text":"दिष्ट्या वर्धामहे सर्वे दिष्ट्या शान्तः पुरोचनः ।\nदिष्ट्या मम परं दुःखमपनीतं महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune we prosper, by good fortune Purochana is dead, and by good fortune my great sorrow is removed, O radiant one."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"ततो जगाम विदुरो धृतराष्ट्रस्य शासनात् ।\nसकाशं यज्ञसेनस्य पाण्डवानां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, at Dhritarashtra's command, Vidura set out for the presence of Yajnasena and the Pandavas, O Bharata."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्र गत्वा स धर्मज्ञः सर्वशास्त्रविशारदः ।\nद्रुपदं न्यायतो राजन्संयुक्तमुपतस्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arriving there, he who knew dharma and was skilled in all the scriptures approached Drupada, who was waiting as propriety required."}},{"n":9,"text":"स चापि प्रतिजग्राह धर्मेण विदुरं ततः ।\nचक्रतुश्च यथान्यायं कुशलप्रश्नसंविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drupada received Vidura in turn with due honor, and they exchanged inquiries of welfare as custom demands."}},{"n":10,"text":"ददर्श पाण्डवांस्तत्र वासुदेवं च भारत ।\nस्नेहात्परिष्वज्य स तान्पप्रच्छानामयं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Vidura saw the Pandavas and Vasudeva, embraced them affectionately and asked after their health."}},{"n":11,"text":"तैश्चाप्यमितबुद्धिः स पूजितोऽथ यथाक्रमम् ।\nवचनाद्धृतराष्ट्रस्य स्नेहयुक्तं पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of boundless wisdom, he was honored by them in due order."}},{"n":12,"text":"पप्रच्छानामयं राजंस्ततस्तान्पाण्डुनन्दनान् ।\nप्रददौ चापि रत्नानि विविधानि वसूनि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Dhritarashtra's name he again and again asked the sons of Pandu about their well-being, and presented them with jewels and wealth of many kinds."}},{"n":13,"text":"पाण्डवानां च कुन्त्याश्च द्रौपद्याश्च विशां पते ।\nद्रुपदस्य च पुत्राणां यथा दत्तानि कौरवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gave the gifts the Kauravas had sent to the Pandavas, to Kunti, to Draupadi and to the sons of Drupada, O lord of the people."}},{"n":14,"text":"प्रोवाच चामितमतिः प्रश्रितं विनयान्वितः ।\nद्रुपदं पाण्डुपुत्राणां संनिधौ केशवस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vidura of boundless wisdom, humble and courteous, spoke to Drupada in the presence of the Pandava sons and Keshava."}},{"n":15,"text":"राजञ्शृणु सहामात्यः सपुत्रश्च वचो मम ।\nधृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्रस्त्वां सहामात्यः सबान्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear my words, O king, together with your ministers and sons. Dhritarashtra, with his sons, ministers and kinsmen, sends you greetings."}},{"n":16,"text":"अब्रवीत्कुशलं राजन्प्रीयमाणः पुनः पुनः ।\nप्रीतिमांस्ते दृढं चापि संबन्धेन नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"He asks after your welfare again and again with delight, O king, and is firmly pleased at the bond of marriage with you."}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा भीष्मः शांतनवः कौरवैः सह सर्वशः ।\nकुशलं त्वां महाप्राज्ञः सर्वतः परिपृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too the wise Bhishma son of Shantanu, together with the Kauravas, inquires after your welfare in every way."}},{"n":18,"text":"भारद्वाजो महेष्वासो द्रोणः प्रियसखस्तव ।\nसमाश्लेषमुपेत्य त्वां कुशलं परिपृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona son of Bharadvaja, the great archer and your dear friend, embraces you in spirit and asks after your well-being."}},{"n":19,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रश्च पाञ्चाल्य त्वया संबन्धमीयिवान् ।\nकृतार्थं मन्यतेऽऽत्मानं तथा सर्वेऽपि कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra, O Panchala, regards himself as fulfilled by the connection with you, and so do all the Kauravas."}},{"n":20,"text":"न तथा राज्यसंप्राप्तिस्तेषां प्रीतिकरी मता ।\nयथा संबन्धकं प्राप्य यज्ञसेन त्वया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gaining the kingdom did not please them so much, O Yajnasena, as gaining this alliance with you."}},{"n":21,"text":"एतद्विदित्वा तु भवान्प्रस्थापयतु पाण्डवान् ।\nद्रष्टुं हि पाण्डुदायादांस्त्वरन्ते कुरवो भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, please send the Pandavas on their way, for the Kurus are most eager to see the heirs of Pandu."}},{"n":22,"text":"विप्रोषिता दीर्घकालमिमे चापि नरर्षभाः ।\nउत्सुका नगरं द्रष्टुं भविष्यन्ति पृथा तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"These bulls among men have long been away, and they too will be eager to see their city, as will Pritha."}},{"n":23,"text":"कृष्णामपि च पाञ्चालीं सर्वाः कुरुवरस्त्रियः ।\nद्रष्टुकामाः प्रतीक्षन्ते पुरं च विषयं च नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the noble women of the Kuru house also wait, longing to see Krishna of Panchala, and our city and country as well."}},{"n":24,"text":"स भवान्पाण्डुपुत्राणामाज्ञापयतु माचिरम् ।\nगमनं सहदाराणामेतदागमनं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"So give the command without delay for the Pandavas to depart with their wife; that is why I have come."}},{"n":25,"text":"विसृष्टेषु त्वया राजन्पाण्डवेषु महात्मसु ।\nततोऽहं प्रेषयिष्यामि धृतराष्ट्रस्य शीघ्रगान् ।\nआगमिष्यन्ति कौन्तेयाः कुन्ती च सह कृष्णया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once you have let the great Pandavas go, I will send swift messengers to Dhritarashtra, and the sons of Kunti will arrive with Kunti and Krishna."}}]}]}